abstract: >-
  The TAP-721 family: TAP-721 (proposal name; number 721 requested), a flagship TapeOut standard for
  Netlist-Bound NFTs, three extension TAPs (bridging between TapeOut chains, Proof-of-Design attributes,
  and a structural hash of flat netlists, now with version 2 for tapnet/2), and the related drafts
  TAP-5375 Design Credits and Lineage and TAP-5192 Soulbound Netlist Credentials, with Python reference
  implementations, test vectors, Foundry contracts and tools. TAP-7007 Large Netlists and Verifiable
  Execution is kept in its own repository (BruceLanLan/tap-large-netlists). Submitted to
  TapeOutProtocol/TAPs on 2026-10-18 (Idea issue #66, PRs #67-#70) and 2026-10-21 (core and structural
  hash revisions; Idea issues #71-#73, PRs #74-#76); all PRs ready for review. The bodies of #67-#70 pin
  commit a39f30b of this repository. Draft; not deployed; reviewed internally only, not externally
  audited.
